---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;

const points = [
  {
    title: "Judged once, in the background",
    body: "Each new mail from the rule's senders is checked after sync. Add a sender and choose whether the last 30 days are checked too.",
  },
  {
    title: "Your own subscription",
    body: "Runs on the Claude Pro/Max or SuperGrok seat you connected for drafts. No API key, no per-token bill.",
  },
  {
    title: "Stays out of your way",
    body: "A verdict never touches snoozed, follow-up or reply-later mail, and never pulls archived mail back out.",
  },
];
---

<section class="px-6 py-24 md:py-32" id="ai-rules">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-landing">
    <div class="reveal grid items-end gap-6 md:grid-cols-12 md:gap-16">
      <div class="md:col-span-7">
        <p
          class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-accent"
        >
          AI Rules
        </p>
        <h2
          class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold leading-[1.15] tracking-tight text-balance text-ink md:text-[2.75rem]"
        >
          Sort mail by what it says, not just who sent it.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <p
        class="reveal reveal-delay-1 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-light md:col-span-5"
      >
        Some senders mix the mail you want with the mail you don't. Describe
        the good ones in plain language, and a model reads each new message
        and files it where it belongs.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div
      class="reveal reveal-delay-2 mt-14 grid overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-surface-200 bg-white md:grid-cols-12"
    >
      <div class="px-8 py-8 md:col-span-7 md:px-10 md:py-10">
        <p
          class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ink-muted"
        >
          What should the model look for?
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 font-display text-2xl leading-snug text-ink md:text-[1.75rem]">
          &ldquo;An assignment with two remote days a week, on-site in Uppsala
          or Stockholm&rdquo;
        </p>

        <p
          class="mt-8 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ink-muted"
        >
          Mail from
        </p>
        <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          <span
            class="rounded-full border border-surface-200 bg-surface-50 px-3 py-1 font-mono text-sm text-ink"
            >consult.example</span
          >
          <span
            class="rounded-full border border-surface-200 bg-surface-50 px-3 py-1 font-mono text-sm text-ink"
            >anna@brokers.example</span
          >
        </div>

        <dl class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-surface-200 px-4 py-3">
            <dt class="text-xs text-ink-muted">When it matches</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1 font-medium text-ink">File in Imbox</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-surface-200 px-4 py-3">
            <dt class="text-xs text-ink-muted">When it does not match</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1 font-medium text-ink">Block (archive)</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>

      <div
        class="flex flex-col justify-center border-t border-surface-200 bg-ink px-8 py-10 md:col-span-5 md:border-l md:border-t-0 md:px-10"
      >
        <p
          class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-white/65"
        >
          Matched mail
        </p>
        <div
          class="mt-3 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5"
        >
          <div class="border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-3">
            <p class="text-sm font-medium text-white">
              Senior developer, 6 months, Stockholm
            </p>
            <p class="mt-0.5 text-xs text-white/50">
              Anna Berg &middot; Filed in Imbox
            </p>
          </div>
          <p class="px-4 py-3.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/80">
            On-site in Stockholm three days a week, remote the other two.
            Matches the criterion.
          </p>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/70">
          Every match shows where it went and the model's reason, on the AI
          Rules page and on the mail itself.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <ul class="mt-10 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">
      {
        points.map((p, i) => (
          <li class={`reveal reveal-delay-${i + 1}`}>
            <h3 class="font-sans text-lg font-bold text-ink">{p.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-ink-light">{p.body}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>

    <p class="reveal mt-10 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
      Mail from the senders a rule covers is sent to Anthropic or xAI to be
      judged. Nothing else is. Needs a connected model, see
      <a
        href={`${base}docs/draft-generation`}
        class="text-accent underline-offset-2 hover:underline">Draft Generation</a
      >.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
